Gates: CI/CD Pipeline Mapping

Spec: CicdPipeline

Purpose:
  Canonical mapping of the security-first CI/CD PR pipeline to SDD
  gates, stages, and the scanner catalog. Target projects'
  pipeline configs (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Jenkins...) MUST
  instantiate this ORDER — SDDRA defines WHAT and in WHICH ORDER;
  the pipeline config defines HOW (tooling syntax).

Owns: gates/cicd-pipeline.sdd

Scope:
  Spec-level mapping only — NO pipeline implementation lives here
  (out of scope: YAML/Workflow files; each target project owns its
  config, instantiated from this mapping).

Pipeline (canonical order — security before completion, mirroring
DL1 v2 ordering):

  PR received
    |
  1  Dependency Check .... DEPENDENCY_GATE
    |                        @dependency-gate.sdd (intake decision)
  2  SAST / SCA .......... SEC.SAST + SEC.DEP
    |                        @../security/scanners.sdd
  3  Secret Detection .... SEC.SECRET
    |                        @../security/scanners.sdd
  4  Lint ............... CODE-QUALITY-GATE
    |                        @../testing/CODE-QUALITY-GATE.sdd
  5  Unit Test ........... testing gates (unit level)
    |                        @../testing/gates.sdd, levels.sdd
  6  Integration Test .... testing gates (integration level)
    |                        @../testing/gates.sdd
  7  Security Scan ...... SC stage (scoped instances)
    |                        @../stages/SC.sdd, stage/gates.sdd
  8  Container Scan ..... SEC.CONTAINER
    |                        @../security/scanners.sdd
  9  Infrastructure Scan . SEC.IAC
    |                        @../security/scanners.sdd (Terraform/
    |                        Kubernetes security)
 10  Code Review Gate ... CR stage (peer review)
    |                        @../workflow/step-keys.sdd
    |                        (CRScopedSemantics)
 11  BUILD .............. build gates
    |                        @infrastructure.sdd
 12  DEPLOY ............. release gates + DO stage
                             @release.sdd, ../stages/DO.sdd

MappingRationale:

  - Steps 1-3 run BEFORE code-quality steps: a dependency or secret
    failure is the cheapest possible failure — it never reaches
    test compute ([R101] security-first work ordering).
  - Step 7 (Security Scan) mirrors DL1 v2: scoped security precedes
    test COMPLETION (unit/integration may run in parallel, but the
    PR cannot complete without SC pass — No Security Pass -> No
    Test Completion).
  - Steps 8-9 protect the artifacts and infrastructure the build
    will produce.
  - Step 10 (Code Review Gate) is the human/peer gate before build
    resources are spent ([G11] AI cannot waive).
  - DAST (SEC.DAST) runs POST-DEPLOY on staging — not a PR gate; it
    feeds the incident/observability loop
    (@../observability/INDEX.sdd).

Rules:

  [CC1] This mapping is CANONICAL — CI configurations in target
        projects MUST instantiate this order; reordering security
        checks after completion checks is a drift violation
        (@../queries/drift-detection.sdd).
  [CC2] Every pipeline stage in a target project MUST cite its SDD
        gate/scanner source — uncited stages are orphan pipeline
        steps (drift).
  [CC3] Pipeline ordering is security-first, mirroring DL1 v2 —
        security precedes test completion in every layer of the
        system (delivery chain AND CI/CD).
  [CC4] Gate failures block subsequent stages ([GT4]) — a failing
        Dependency Check never proceeds to SAST compute.
  [CC5] Waivers follow gate policy (@policy.sdd [GT9]-[GT10]) —
        with Reason, Owner, Expiration; AI cannot waive ([G11]).

Navigation:
  GatesIndex: @INDEX.sdd
  DependencyGate: @dependency-gate.sdd
  Scanners: @../security/scanners.sdd
  TestingGates: @../testing/gates.sdd
  CodeQualityGate: @../testing/CODE-QUALITY-GATE.sdd
  SecurityStage: @../stages/SC.sdd
  StepKeys: @../workflow/step-keys.sdd
  DeliveryChain: @../chains/delivery.sdd (v2 ordering)
  ReleaseGates: @release.sdd
  DriftDetection: @../queries/drift-detection.sdd

State: +
  (Phase 155: created as the spec-level CI/CD mapping from the
   security-first pipeline proposal; scanner catalog extended with
   SEC.IAC (checkov, tfsec, kube-linter); pipeline implementation
   itself remains per-project config)
